---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import "../styles/chronicles.css";
---

<Base
  title="AI Research & Benchmarks — The Agent Chronicles"
  description="Systems benchmarks, token economics, and TLS edge forensics by Aswath S."
>
  <Nav currentPath="/research/" />

  <main class="s page-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">SYSTEMS RESEARCH · BENCHMARKS · FORENSICS</div>
      <h1 class="page-title">AI Research & Benchmarks</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">
        Empirical studies on agent token economics, TLS transport fingerprinting, and automated vulnerability forensics.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Study 1: Token Tax -->
    <article class="research-paper">
      <div class="paper-meta">
        <span class="paper-tag">EMPIRICAL BENCHMARK</span>
        <span class="paper-date">Published 2026-11-10</span>
      </div>
      <h2>The Token Tax: Programmatic Tool Execution (Code Mode) vs. Traditional JSON Function Calling</h2>
      <div class="paper-authors">By Aswath S · Agent Systems Desk</div>

      <div class="paper-body">
        <h3>Abstract</h3>
        <p>
          Model Context Protocol (MCP) and JSON function calling dominate modern agent-tool interfaces. However, for data-intensive retrieval (e.g. search listings, paginated catalogs), traditional tool-calling introduces severe token inflation by serializing raw JSON arrays directly into the conversational context. We measured token spend, round-trip latency, and reasoning degradation across a 60-item search workload. Replacing multi-turn JSON tool-calling with an in-memory programmatic execution harness (Code Mode) reduced ingested context from <b>32,450 tokens to 142 tokens</b> (a 99.5% reduction) while decreasing end-to-end latency from 4.8s to 1.1s.
        </p>

        <div class="findings-box">
          <h4>Key Findings</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><b>The Schema Tax:</b> Large APIs (e.g. Cloudflare's 2,500 endpoints) consume over 1,000,000 tokens purely in JSON Schema definitions. Code Mode compresses the entire API surface down to ~1,000 tokens of typed declarations.</li>
            <li><b>The Pagination Trap:</b> Paginating 3 pages across an MCP server requires 3 discrete conversational turns, incurring 3x network round-trip overhead and filling the LLM context with irrelevant records.</li>
            <li><b>In-Memory Filtering:</b> Moving filtering, sorting, and deduplication logic into local RAM guarantees that only finalized answer strings enter the context window.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="paper-actions">
          <a href="https://github.com/aswathas/olx-car-search/blob/main/docs/code-mode/02-options.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="paper-btn">Read Full Spec & Ledger ➔</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Study 2: TLS Fingerprinting -->
    <article class="research-paper">
      <div class="paper-meta">
        <span class="paper-tag">TRANSPORT FORENSICS</span>
        <span class="paper-date">Published 2026-11-09</span>
      </div>
      <h2>TLS ClientHello Fingerprinting at the Edge: Why Headless Scrapers Fail Before HTTP</h2>
      <div class="paper-authors">By Aswath S · Agent Systems Desk</div>

      <div class="paper-body">
        <h3>Summary</h3>
        <p>
          Investigating connection resets and <code>ERR_HTTP2_PROTOCOL_ERROR</code> encountered when querying modern web marketplaces (OLX India). While developers instinctively suspect IP rate-limits or User-Agent detection—frequently turning to expensive paid proxy services—forensic packet inspection reveals the block occurs during the initial TLS handshake.
        </p>
        <p>
          Edge protection services (Cloudflare, Akamai) analyze the cipher suite order, supported elliptic curves, and extensions in the <code>ClientHello</code> packet. Python <code>requests</code>, <code>httpx</code>, and headless Chrome emit distinct signatures that are dropped with connection resets before a single byte of HTTP payload arrives. Bypassing this layer requires TLS-level socket impersonation (<code>curl_cffi</code> with Chrome handshake), achieving 100% success at ₹0 infrastructure cost.
        </p>

        <div class="paper-actions">
          <a href="https://github.com/aswathas/olx-car-search/blob/main/SPEC.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="paper-btn">Read TLS Edge Analysis ➔</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Study 3: 298-Case Routing Benchmark -->
    <article class="research-paper">
      <div class="paper-meta">
        <span class="paper-tag">ROUTER TAXONOMY BENCHMARK</span>
        <span class="paper-date">Published 2026-11-08</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Hierarchical Intent Resolution: Evaluating 2-Tier Taxonomies vs. Flat Semantic Search Across 298 Test Cases</h2>
      <div class="paper-authors">By Aswath S · Agent Systems Desk</div>

      <div class="paper-body">
        <h3>Summary</h3>
        <p>
          As an agent's skill library expands to thousands of tools, flat embedding vector search suffers from high semantic collision rates on ambiguous user queries. We developed a hierarchical 2-tier classification router coupled with an outcome-driven learning loop.
        </p>
        <p>
          Evaluated against a curated 298-case adversarial benchmark suite, the 2-tier router achieved <b>99.2% Top-1 accuracy</b> (compared to 71.4% for flat cosine similarity), while executing in under 4.5ms without injecting permanent tokens into the LLM system prompt.
        </p>
        <div class="paper-actions">
          <a href="https://github.com/aswathas/skill-router" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="paper-btn">View skill-router Benchmark &amp; Evals ➔</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .page-container {
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    border-bottom: 3px double var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--red);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .page-title {
    font-family: "Archivo Black", sans-serif;
    font-size: 2.8rem;
    line-height: 1;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .page-lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--grey);
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .research-paper {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .paper-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .paper-tag {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    padding: 3px 8px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .paper-date {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--grey);
  }
  .research-paper h2 {
    font-family: "Archivo Black", sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .paper-authors {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--red);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .paper-body h3 {
    font-family: "Archivo Black", sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-top: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .paper-body p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .findings-box {
    background: var(--paper2);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .findings-box h4 {
    font-family: "Archivo Black", sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .findings-box ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .findings-box li {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .paper-actions {
    margin-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(20, 18, 16, 0.15);
    padding-top: 16px;
  }
  .paper-btn {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .paper-btn:hover {
    color: var(--red);
  }
</style>
